>> title: Carnitas
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: pork, mexican, oven, tacos, braise
>> counters: Taquería
>> aka: taco de carnitas, carnitas taco, roast pork
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas, salsa-roja, refried-beans
>> servings: 8
>> time: 4 hr
>> step.4: braise 300°F 3 hr
>> step.5: shred, crisp under the broiler 10 min

Preheat the #oven{} to 300°F (150°C).

Toss @pork shoulder{4%lb}(1.8 kg; cut in 2-in chunks), @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @dried oregano{1%tsp} in a #Dutch oven{}.

Add @lard{1/2%cup}(110 g), @orange{1}(halved), @white onion{1}(quartered), @garlic{6%cloves}, @bay leaves{2}, @water{2%cup}(475 mL) to @&(~1)seasoned pork{}.

Braise @&(~1)pot{} covered at 300°F until fork-tender, ~{3%hr}.

Shred @&(~1)braised pork{} and crisp it in its fat under the #broiler{} for ~{10%min}.
